From 7a159f88521cb78f940a3de6fca640c0912ad556 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pdale-boop <237306950+pdale-boop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:27:27 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Characters: Wind Waker HD's clouds on the characters' light,
 and its cloud floor from the clock

Characters: Wind Waker HD's clouds on the characters' light, and its cloud floor at night

Wind Waker HD dims the characters' sunlight under its cloud shadows: the light is mix(shade, lit, ramp x cloud),
cloud = clamp(its cloud texture at the pixel's world position + the floor). The characters now read the same
texture, drift and floor as the scenery's cloud shadows on HD's rule (post_fx::actor_cloud_source,
post_fx::cloud_hd_floor), so both darken under the same cloud; with HD's cloud shadows off or no HD cloud texture
the characters take 1. The floor is now HD's, 1 - max(0.25, 0.9 x the sun's height), for scenery and characters
(0.364 at 10:00, 0.131 at noon, 0.75 at night: clouds still dim lit places a little at night, as in HD).
DOL_AURORA_ACTOR_LIGHT_DEBUG=6 shows the characters' cloud term.

gxcore tests: cloud = 1 reproduces the traced HD pixels exactly; cloud = 0 gives the hemisphere colour. In game at
Outset's pier with the clouds repeated finely, Link takes the texture's average (0.91) and the scenery dims with him.

Aurora: Wind Waker HD's cloud floor from the host's clock (aurora_set_cloud_hd_floor)

The cloud shadows on HD's rule take clamp(texel + floor), and HD works the floor out from the clock in setSunpos:
1 - max(0.25, -0.9 cos(time - 15 degrees)). cloud_hd_floor() worked it out from the shadow light's height
instead, which is the same thing only for the true sun. With HD's light rule (aurora_set_sun_hd_light) the light
is held at 40,000 high before 09:00 and after 17:00, so the floor came out 0.596 at 07:30, 18:30 and 20:00 where
HD's is 0.75 (uf[2].y in an HD capture, at all three hours), and 0.248 at noon against HD's 0.131: at dawn
and dusk a cloud took about 1.6 times HD's light from Link and the scenery.

aurora_set_cloud_hd_floor(floor): the host's floor from the clock, used by the scenery and the characters while
it is set; a negative value goes back to the light's height. DOL_AURORA_CLOUD_SHADOWS_HD_POWER still overrides
both. The comments that gave 0.364 and 0.1307 as the light-height rule's now say where they hold.

The post_fx modules compile with Dawn (Vulkan, core and compatibility); the gxcore and runtime tests pass.
